{"id":"b2cc87480438176a","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-df-sylow.md","title":"Sylow Subgroups","display":"df-sylow — Sylow Subgroups","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-sylow","aliases":["58-df-sylow"],"display":"df-sylow — Sylow Subgroups","depends_on":["[[../batch08/58-df-p-group.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-sylow"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-sylow</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-sylow — Sylow Subgroups"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ac978c566ec8e658\" href=\"?note=ac978c566ec8e658\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-p-group.md\">../batch08/58-df-p-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"59685d062adf2748\" href=\"?note=59685d062adf2748\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md\">../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,\\cdot_G,P,p\\in V\">\\(G,\\cdot_G,P,p\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S,\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S,\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sylow}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G,p)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(P,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(P\\times P),p)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall H\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(H,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(H\\times H),p)\n\\land P\\subseteq H\n\\to H=P\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sylow}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G,p)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(P,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(P\\times P),p)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall H\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(H,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(H\\times H),p)\n\\land P\\subseteq H\n\\to H=P\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the maximal-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>-subgroup definition; for finite <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span> it is equivalent to the usual order-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p^a\">\\(p^a\\)</span> formulation.</li>\n<li>Sylow (1872): existence, conjugacy, divisibility by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_p(G) = |G : N_G(P)|\">\\(n_p(G) = |G : N_G(P)|\\)</span> for any Sylow <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Hall's theorem (1928): solvable groups have Hall <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p&#39;\">\\(p&#39;\\)</span>-subgroups.</li>\n<li>Burnside's <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p^aq^b\">\\(p^aq^b\\)</span> theorem says that every finite group whose order has only two prime divisors is solvable; its isomorphism type is not determined by those primes alone.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch08/58-df-p-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ac978c566ec8e658","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-p-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md","status":"resolved","id":"59685d062adf2748","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"G,\\cdot_G,P,p\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S,\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sylow}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{SylowSubgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G,p)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(P,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(P,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(P\\times P),p)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall H\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,G,\\cdot_G)\n\\land\\mathrm{PGroupStructure}_S(H,\\cdot_G\\upharpoonright(H\\times H),p)\n\\land P\\subseteq H\n\\to H=P\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"p^a","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"n_p(G) = |G : N_G(P)|","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"p'","display":false},{"tex":"p^aq^b","display":false}],"bytes":1332,"backlinks":[{"id":"b4756908c8b755cf","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1273","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-sylow.md|58-df-sylow]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["ac978c566ec8e658","59685d062adf2748"]}